<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-6">6 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Philip II of France takes Château Gaillard</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">French troops captured Richard the Lionheart's great castle above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a> after a six-month siege, some climbing in through a latrine chute. Normandy fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> within months.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-12">12 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Fourth Crusade storms Constantinople</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusaders</a> and Venetians broke into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> and began three days of pillage. They set up a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-empire">Latin Empire</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> never recovered its former strength.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-i-latin-emperor" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baldwin-i-latin-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-16">16 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Baldwin I is crowned first emperor of the Latin Empire</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Baldwin, Count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> and a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>, was crowned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a> as the first emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-empire">Latin Empire</a>. In 1205 the Bulgarian tsar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaloyan-of-bulgaria">Kaloyan</a> defeated and captured him at Adrianople.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-i-latin-emperor">Baldwin I, Latin Emperor</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/boniface-i-marquis-of-montferrat" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boniface-i-marquis-of-montferrat.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-12">12 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Venice acquires Crete from Boniface of Montferrat</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Venetians acquired <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boniface-i-marquis-of-montferrat">Boniface of Montferrat</a>, leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>, forestalling their Genoese rivals. Boniface sold it for 1,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> marks, a share of the island's revenues and Venetian support for his bid for the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessalonica</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boniface-i-marquis-of-montferrat">Boniface I, Marquis of Montferrat</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chakirmaut">Battle of Chakirmaut</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Chakirmaut was fought in 1204 in western Mongolia between Temüjin, the future Genghis Khan, and the Naimans under Tayang Khan, who were joined by Jamukha and other opponents of Temüjin.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-andkhud">Battle of Andkhud</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Andkhud was fought in 1204 near Andkhoy in northern Afghanistan, where an army of the Khwarazmshah Muhammad II, reinforced by the Qara Khitai, crushed the Ghurid sultan Mu'izz al-Din Muhammad, who escaped with difficulty.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Siege</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/sack-of-constantinople-1204">Sack of Constantinople (1204)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The sack of Constantinople in 1204 was the capture and plunder of the Byzantine capital by the army of the Fourth Crusade, supported by Venice.</p></div></li></ol></section>
