<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/byzantine-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Byzantine%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Byzantine Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Fourth Crusade sacks Constantinople and founds a Latin Empire</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/ghurid-sultanate"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ghurid%20Sultanate.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ghurid Sultanate</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Khwarazmshah and the Qara Khitai defeat Mu'izz al-Din at Andkhud</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-venice"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Venice.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Venice</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Fourth Crusade, led by Doge Enrico Dandolo, takes Constantinople</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/county-of-flanders"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/County%20of%20Flanders.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>County of Flanders</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Baldwin IX becomes the first Latin emperor of Constantinople</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/county-of-hainaut"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/County%20of%20Hainaut.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>County of Hainaut</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Count Baldwin VI becomes the first Latin emperor of Constantinople</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/duchy-of-normandy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Duchy%20of%20Normandy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Duchy of Normandy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Philip II of France takes Château Gaillard and Rouen and annexes Normandy</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/bailiwick-of-jersey"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Bailiwick%20of%20Jersey.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Bailiwick of Jersey</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">King John loses Normandy, but Jersey stays with the English crown</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-georgia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Georgia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Georgia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Georgian-backed Komnenos brothers found the Empire of Trebizond</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/empire-of-trebizond"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Empire%20of%20Trebizond.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Empire of Trebizond</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Alexios and David Komnenos seize Trebizond with Georgian troops</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/language/mongolian"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mongolian.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mongolian</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Genghis Khan adopts a script for the Mongolian language, adapted from the Uyghur alphabet</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/hagia-sophia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hagia%20Sophia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hagia Sophia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Crusaders sack Constantinople, and the church becomes a Latin Catholic cathedral until 1261</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/latin-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Latin%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Latin Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The crusaders capture and plunder Constantinople, elect Baldwin I emperor on 9 May and crown him in the Hagia Sophia on 16 May</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/constantinople"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Constantinople.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Constantinople</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Fourth Crusade takes and plunders the city, and the Latin Empire holds it until 1261</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/venice"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Venice.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Venice</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Venetians and French crusaders capture and sack Constantinople, and Venice takes territories in the Aegean, including Crete</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/dublin"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dublin.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dublin</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">King John orders the founding of Dublin Castle</span></li></ul></section>
